    "explanation": "By (a), each term is a difference: $\\frac{1}{1 \\times 2} = 1 - \\frac{1}{2}$, $\\frac{1}{2 \\times 3} = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3}$, and so on. Adding, the middle fractions cancel and the sum is $1 - \\frac{1}{10} = \\frac{9}{10}$. In general the sum is $1 - \\frac{1}{n + 1}$, and $1 - \\frac{1}{n + 1} = 0.95$ gives $n + 1 = 20$, so $n = 19$.",
    "workedSolution": "**(a)** Common denominator $x(x + 1)$: $\\frac{x + 1 - x}{x(x + 1)} = \\frac{1}{x(x + 1)}$.\n\n**(b)** $\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{2}\\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3}\\right) + \\cdots + \\left(\\frac{1}{9} - \\frac{1}{10}\\right)$ **(M1)** $= 1 - \\frac{1}{10} = \\frac{9}{10}$ **(A1)**.\n\n**(c)** The sum to $n$ terms is $1 - \\frac{1}{n + 1}$. So $\\frac{1}{n + 1} = 0.05$ **(M1)**, $n + 1 = 20$ and $n = 19$ **(A1)**.",
